B = [
('Singapore Airlines','Southeast Asia','1970s-present','airline','In the style of Singapore Airlines, serene, polished, premium design in deep midnight navy and warm saffron gold. A stylised golden bird emblem of layered, upswept feather strokes sits on solid navy panels or crisp white fields. Large clean sans-serif capitals in navy or white are spaced generously and set in two stacked lines. Surfaces are glossy lacquer, pearly white and soft metallic gold foil, with fine batik-like flowing pattern in muted gold on navy as a quiet secondary motif. Colour blocking is calm and symmetrical, with a broad navy band against white and a thin gold accent line. Mood is hospitable, graceful, luxurious and impeccably tidy.'),
('KLM','Europe','1960s-present','airline','In the style of KLM, cheerful, friendly, confident Dutch design in a single bright sky blue against clean white. A small crown emblem topped with a cross sits above bold, wide, upright sans-serif capitals, shown in blue on white or reversed in white on blue. The signature is flat colour blocking with a large sweep of cornflower or azure, sometimes broken by thin horizontal pinstripes in two blues, and a round badge version in navy with white lettering. Finishes are glossy enamel and clean matte paint with crisp edges. Palette stays disciplined with sky blue, white, navy and a rare touch of orange. Mood is optimistic, open, tidy and approachable.'),
('SAS','Europe','1970s-90s','airline','In the style of SAS, crisp, Nordic, functional design in deep ultramarine blue with clean white. Heavy italic slab-like capitals lean forward with tightly joined letters, often shown in navy on white, set above a smaller line of regular sans-serif lettering. Colour blocking is broad and quiet, with a dark blue field, pale grey or white areas and one thin stripe set. A bold stripe motif in red, yellow and blue, each band equal in width, runs diagonally or horizontally as a lively accent against the reserved base. Finishes are satin paint, brushed light metal and smooth laminate, with a restrained, democratic, design-led Scandinavian rigour and no ornament.'),
('Swissair','Europe','1950s-90s','airline','In the style of Swissair, rigorous Swiss International Style design built on pure red and white. A bold red field carries a white square-armed cross, and a slanted parallelogram of red cuts diagonally across white surfaces as a crisp shape. Lettering is lowercase, heavy, tight Helvetica-like grotesque in red or white, flush left, with immaculate spacing and a grid-based layout. Finishes are glossy enamel and flat printed colour with sharp edges, set against bare white with generous empty space. A secondary palette of dark grey, silver and black is used sparingly for fine rules and small captions. Mood is precise, neutral, clean, trustworthy and timelessly modernist.'),
('Air India','South Asia','1960s-present','airline','In the style of Air India, warm, ornate, richly coloured design with a regal Indian character. Strong red and white colour blocking is paired with deep maroon, saffron, aubergine and burnished gold. A small arched motif drawn from ornamental scalloped arches and a gold circular emblem repeats as a graphic mark, often with fine curved lines that suggest a sun or a gateway frame. Lettering is wide, clean, slightly rounded sans-serif in white on red or red on white, with italic touches. Surfaces are glossy lacquer and gold foil, with jewel-like borders, paisley, jali lattice and floral geometry as pattern. Mood is hospitable, festive, theatrical and proudly decorative.'),
('JAL','East Asia','1960s-present','airline','In the style of JAL, minimal, refined, precise Japanese design in one vivid vermilion red with white and charcoal. A solid red circle, like the rising sun, holds a white stylised crane drawn with a single sweeping curved neck and few feather strokes, a flat emblem of confident simplicity. Lettering is bold, rounded, upright sans-serif capitals in red, grey or black, with wide stretched proportions and perfect spacing. Colour blocking is a clean white ground with one strong red shape, sometimes a dark grey band beneath it. Finishes are glossy lacquer and flat matte print with very crisp edges. Mood is calm, elegant, orderly, graphic and quietly dignified.'),
('Aeroflot','Russia and Eastern Europe','1960s-80s','airline','In the style of Aeroflot, Soviet-era graphic confidence in deep cobalt navy, pale sky blue, white and a punchy red. A circular emblem with outspread, feathered bars on both sides sits centred over a small disc, drawn flat in navy or silver-grey. Lettering is Cyrillic capitals, wide and sturdy with sharp angular strokes and long dashed rules beneath. Colour blocking is bold and optimistic, with sweeping diagonals, a broad pale blue band across bare metallic silver or white, and red used as a decisive accent. Surfaces are polished aluminium, flat gouache-like colour and slightly worn enamel. Flat graphic geometry, rounded rectangles and radiating lines give an idealistic, mid-century modern, utilitarian feel.'),
('Concorde','Europe','1970s','aircraft','In the style of Concorde, needle-sharp, futuristic, elegant design in gleaming white. Long narrow forms taper to a point, with a sleek elongated triangle silhouette used as a repeated graphic shape. Surfaces are bright reflective white gloss, polished silver and pale grey metal with a heat-resistant ceramic sheen, kept clear of clutter. A single narrow cobalt or navy cheatline runs the full length of a form, with fine red and blue accent flashes on small panels. Lettering is small, spaced, lowercase or capital sans-serif in dark blue or black. Seamless and streamlined, the palette stays almost entirely white and silver. Mood is exclusive, rapid, optimistic and 1970s high-tech.'),
('Boeing','North America','1960s-present','aircraft','In the style of Boeing, clean, confident, engineered corporate design in rich cobalt blue, deep navy and crisp white. Broad colour blocking uses a dark blue base rising into a pale blue field, divided by a smooth flowing curve with a soft gradient and a single sharp swoosh of light blue. Lettering is widely spaced, bold, italic or slanted sans-serif capitals in blue or white, paired with a small circle-and-slash emblem. Finishes are glossy enamel and satin metal with perfectly smooth, seamless surfaces, plus fine technical line graphics. Mood is dependable, large-scale, precise, optimistic and industrial, with a clear and modern engineering feel.'),
('Airbus','Europe','1990s-present','aircraft','In the style of Airbus, smooth, calm, composed European design in a restrained palette of deep royal blue, bright cyan, pale sky blue and clean white. Soft gradients fade from dark blue to light blue across large curved panels, divided by sharp-edged light cyan rays or a simple abstract slanted letter A set in a circle or square. Lettering is heavy, wide, rounded geometric sans-serif capitals in white on blue or blue on white, with very tight, even tracking. Surfaces are glossy white paint, satin enamel and pearly metallic blue, always seamless and free of decoration. Mood is collaborative, modern, quiet, technical and gently optimistic.'),
]
